# `u` lands on the restored text (vim's u_undoredo; `vim -es`): the
# cursor the change started from when it lies within the changed block
# (`4Gddu` → 4:1, `gg3>>u` → 1:1), else the first changed line.
write a.txt "one\ntwo\nthree\nfour\nfive\nsix\n"
open a.txt
command editor.use_vim
key 4
key G
key d
key d
key G
key u
expect screen contains "Ln 4/6 Col 1"
key g
key g
key 3
key >
key >
key G
key u
expect screen contains "Ln 1/6 Col 1"
